// P03.20 (R7): the answer of satisfiesClone is a function of the type alone.
// N0 holds 1980 levels of slices (the depth cut was at 2000 levels of one type
// body); N40 is 40 named structs above it. The depth used to count the levels
// of the whole query, so `b(x N40)` was rejected when it was checked before
// `a(x N0)` (N0 not cached yet) and accepted after it, and with parallel body
// workers the output depended on scheduling. Both orders, and one and eight
// threads, now give the same output (no error: N0 is cloneable).
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-strict-stress.py 40 order ab > %t.ab.gopp
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-strict-stress.py 40 order ba > %t.ba.gopp
// RUN: %gopp check -check-j=1 --check-error-limit=0 %t.ab.gopp > %t.ab.1 2>&1
// RUN: %gopp check -check-j=1 --check-error-limit=0 %t.ba.gopp > %t.ba.1 2>&1
// RUN: %gopp check -check-j=8 --check-error-limit=0 %t.ab.gopp > %t.ab.8 2>&1
// RUN: %gopp check -check-j=8 --check-error-limit=0 %t.ba.gopp > %t.ba.8 2>&1
// RUN: diff %t.ab.1 %t.ba.1
// RUN: diff %t.ab.1 %t.ab.8
// RUN: diff %t.ba.1 %t.ba.8
// RUN: not grep -q "error" %t.ab.1
package main
